  "interpretation": [
    "The identity/multipath control is strongly improved by receiver equalization as SNR increases, reaching essentially zero mean BER at 30 dB in this finite test set.",
    "The exponential memory case is also substantially improved by FIR equalization at 30 dB, but retains about 27% EVM and about 2.3% mean BER.",
    "The two-scale and power-law memories retain much larger residual error, indicating that a short symbol-spaced FIR does not fully capture the tested memory structure.",
    "These are preliminary local numerical reproductions of the experiment equations; the committed repository runner remains the reproducible source of truth."
  ],
  "caveat": "No intrinsic MIN advantage is claimed. The next comparison must use conventional FIR/IIR and Volterra or memory-polynomial baselines under matched parameter budgets."
